2. ADVANTAGES
======================================================================

• Helps compare algorithms objectively.
• Machine-independent analysis.
• Predicts scalability for large inputs.
• Assists in selecting efficient algorithms.
• Improves performance optimization.

======================================================================
3. DISADVANTAGES
======================================================================

• Big O ignores constant factors.
• Does not represent actual execution time.
• Worst-case analysis may overestimate practical performance.
• Average-case analysis is often difficult to compute.

